WHAT IT IS FOR

    fields::Get_Input_() returns 0 while a screen's input delay runs
    (fields.cpp:161-164) and calls ext::Tick only after it (:167) — so
    while a delay counts down, nothing reaches a client: no state, no
    field list, no picture. The research panel sets a delay of five
    passes of 110 ms (tech.cpp:286, :351-353), and its list reached
    OrionLayer ~550 ms after the engine had built and drawn it — on every
    entry, 66-80 % of the time from the click to the panel (work order
    184, doc/briefs/184-research-timing.md). 42 call sites set a delay
    (1, 2, 3, 5 or 20 passes); every one of those screens is heard
    that much later.

    The change ticks during the delay too, and changes nothing else: the
    delay still returns 0 and still counts down, so the original ignores
    input for exactly as long as before; a field activation that arrives
    meanwhile waits in ext::g_pending_field, which is consumed only after
    the delay, as before. One marker, `OrionLayer, open fix 42.`, on one
    line at the one changed place.

